  <keyword>griddedInterpolant</keyword>
  <short_description>Gridded data interpolant object</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>F = griddedInterpolant(x, v)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>F = griddedInterpolant(x, v, method)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>F = griddedInterpolant(x, v, method, extrapolationMethod)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>F = griddedInterpolant(gridVecs, V)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>F = griddedInterpolant(X1, X2, ..., Xn, V)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>F = griddedInterpolant(V)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Vq = F(xq)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Vq = F(xq1, xq2, ..., xqn)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Vq = F(queryGridVecs)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>x</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a vector of sample points (1-D grid), strictly increasing.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>v</param_name>
      <param_description>sample values at the sample points.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>gridVecs</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a cell array <b>{x1, x2, ..., xn}</b> of grid vectors, one per dimension of <b>V</b>.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>V</param_name>
      <param_description>an array of sample values defined over the grid.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>method</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a character vector: <b>'linear'</b> (default), <b>'nearest'</b>, <b>'previous'</b>, <b>'next'</b>, <b>'pchip'</b>, <b>'cubic'</b>, <b>'spline'</b>, or <b>'makima'</b>.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>extrapolationMethod</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a character vector selecting the extrapolation rule: <b>'linear'</b>, <b>'nearest'</b>, <b>'previous'</b>, <b>'next'</b>, <b>'pchip'</b>, <b>'cubic'</b>, <b>'spline'</b>, <b>'makima'</b>, or <b>'none'</b>. The default matches <b>method</b>.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>F</param_name>
      <param_description>a griddedInterpolant object.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>Vq</param_name>
      <param_description>interpolated values at the query points.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>griddedInterpolant</b> stores gridded sample points and values for repeated interpolation queries.</p>
    <p>The object exposes four properties that can be read and set: <b>GridVectors</b> (a cell array of grid vectors), <b>Values</b>, <b>Method</b>, and <b>ExtrapolationMethod</b>.</p>
    <p>Evaluate the interpolant by calling the object like a function, either with one query array per dimension, or with a single cell array of query grid vectors.</p>
    <p>The <b>'cubic'</b> method uses cubic convolution and requires a grid with uniform spacing; on a non-uniform grid it switches to <b>'spline'</b>. Cubic convolution does not support extrapolation, so query points outside the grid return <b>NaN</b> when <b>ExtrapolationMethod</b> is <b>'cubic'</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>1-D interpolation.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data
      ><![CDATA[F = griddedInterpolant([1 2 3], [10 20 30]);
Vq = F(2.5)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>N-D grid given as a cell of grid vectors.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data
      ><![CDATA[F = griddedInterpolant({1:3, 1:3}, magic(3));
Vq = F(2, 2)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Spline interpolation and property readback.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data
      ><![CDATA[F = griddedInterpolant([1 2 3], [10 20 30], 'spline');
Vq = F(2.5);
F.Method
F.ExtrapolationMethod]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
